The Newberry NWG 55-29 preset uses reference inputs distributed by BoreTHM.
The source attribution recorded by BoreTHM is:
Newberry EGS Demonstration: Well 55-29 Stimulation Data. Cladouhos, T.T.
(AltaRock Energy). Geothermal Data Repository, submission 271.
https://doi.org/10.15121/1357916. CC BY 4.0.
The preset represents model inputs derived from those data.

The field-comparison tables in src/borethm_workbench/evidence/ are derived
from the FORGE 16A and 16B circulation comparisons published with BoreTHM
v1.8.0: its validation guide (CC BY 4.0) and the comparison tables in its
validation records. deploy/build_evidence.py records each source file and
checksum. Changes comprise selection of the published primary comparison
values, conversion to SI units and conversion to JSON. The underlying
measurements keep their source licences, as stated in the BoreTHM sources:
Utah FORGE: Well 16A(78)-32 Drilling Data. McLennan, J., Nash, G., Moore, J.,
Skowron, G. and Woolsey, S. (2021). Geothermal Data Repository, submission
1283. https://doi.org/10.15121/1776602. CC BY 4.0.
Utah FORGE: Well 16A(78)-32 Logs. Gilmour, B., Wooden, J., Pulka, F., Rose,
B., Barker, C. and Borchardt, E. (2021). Geothermal Data Repository,
submission 1292. https://doi.org/10.15121/1777912. CC BY 4.0.
Utah FORGE: Deep Wells Temperature Surveys as of September 2022. Jones, C.
(2022). Geothermal Data Repository, submission 1421.
https://doi.org/10.15121/1893533. CC BY 4.0.
Utah FORGE: Well 16B(78)-32 Drilling Data. McLennan, J., Mock, B.,
Swearingen, L., Baldwin, R., Hodder, M., Vetsak, A., Kuhns, A.T., Breland, J.,
England, K. (2023). Geothermal Data Repository, submission 1516.
https://doi.org/10.15121/1998591. CC BY 4.0.

Built browser packages include React, React DOM, Lucide, Plotly and Three.js.
The build generates THIRD-PARTY-LICENCES.txt in the installed package from
the npm dependencies' licence files. Their licences continue to apply.

BoreTHM is a separate dependency:
O'Callaghan, L. (2026). BoreTHM: models of circulating temperature and
borehole stability for drilling into superhot rock [Computer software].
https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23549104
